TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c03","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"Frames 'positivity constrains zeros' as the Weil-shaped mechanism in miniature — positivity telling zeros where they cannot stand.","checksum":"2520ba65c038f913cc10ae59df863396bd4ed046824a6efd72b97987333001e6","id":"B1","limits":"Miniature: recovers only the classical zero-free line; no strengthening toward RH.","type":"B","x":"positivity→zero-free-line here (3-4-1)","y":"Weil positivity mechanism"},{"buys":"The contradiction becomes physical — negative infinite total energy built from nonnegative strata is impossible — in a way the bare trig identity hides.","checksum":"c5af5cd9d945d39af6605f611278d339a3df21ff2d0791bf624057bb0f7ae925","id":"B2","limits":"Physical language over the same analytic content; the singularity structure (residue −m) is housed, not derived.","type":"B","x":"the pole E₀(σ)~1/(σ−1)","y":"infinite total prime energy at σ=1"},{"checksum":"0ee9153faf375d2e8183b430fa7a3248a03b8e2eaf63677add52470e7ca19092","id":"C1","kind":"question","label":"9c: what stronger geometric positivity could push left of Re(s)=1?","note":"Open research, not a result. Honest labels: the positivity location is exact (identities) + computationally verified; 3-4-1 is classical (cited, re-verified here); 9b/9c are open research, not results.","status":"unstated","type":"C"},{"checksum":"d24343c6f9db2e1caaf937fff4da1b301c2dea566007e227b59965c67dfd8371","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Speculative direction for 9c: deformation-agnostic positivity","note":"The mechanism is deformation-agnostic — for any residue pattern with |R_p|≥0 the deformed log-derivative keeps positive coefficients — so the space of sieve deformations may parametrize the space of admissible positive trig polynomials used in modern zero-free regions. Undeveloped.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"b143d27fc82d46c6657481dc18592f072ab05d3e9073eb5a7c0f1e6db9320a4d","generates":[{"prescription":"Deform the marking rule: prime p marks residues R_p={0} (p=2), {0,−2} (p odd) — n marked if p|n or p|(n+2). Markers stay prime; survivors become a new set.","stage":"deform"},{"prescription":"Run the deformed sieve to x=200000 and check survivors against an independent primality sieve.","stage":"identify survivors"},{"prescription":"Write δ(z)=[∏_{p≤z}(1−1/p)²]·𝔖(z): the first factor →0 (Mertens); read the convergent factor 𝔖(z)→2C₂=1.32032….","stage":"renormalize"}],"honest_boundary":"The algebra is exact, but the passage from 𝔖(z) to π₂(x)~𝔖·x/(log x)² is the UNPROVEN twin prime conjecture (numerical ratio 1.6091 at 2·10⁵ vs conjectured 1.3203 — slow convergence); we verify the algebra (local factors assemble to 𝔖), not the conjecture. The open analytic step is exactly where her program would need its canonical form.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D1","rule":"R_p={0} (p=2), {0,−2} (p odd); δ(z)=∏_{p≤z}(1−|R_p|/p)=[∏(1−1/p)²]·𝔖(z); 𝔖(z)→2C₂=1.32032…; S(x,z)/x→δ(z).","subtitle":"Deformation: the singular series as renormalized total weight","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"deformed sieve survivors ≤200000","expected":"exactly the 2160 twin prime lowers"},{"check":"static z-sieve μ-identity at (z,x)=(13,50000),(30,200000)","expected":"exact"},{"check":"S(x,z)/x vs δ(z) at z=7,x=200000","expected":"0.071430 vs 0.071429"},{"check":"𝔖(z) at z=7,13,30,100","expected":"1.367187, 1.344116, 1.330277, 1.322754 → 1.32032"}]},{"checksum":"c6cfa9b62a07f7e8bdf68bcf29fa2bb82f0161f1b4a54cbeb129aa2be0a43061","generates":[{"prescription":"Read the primitive analytic objects — the von Mangoldt series, log ζ, the finite-z density δ(z) — all manifestly positive.","stage":"locate"},{"prescription":"Factor the face-weights' GF: −ζ′/ζ²=(−ζ′/ζ)·(Σμ(m)m^{−s}) — the signs come entirely from the Möbius factor, i.e. from inclusion–exclusion, not the volume.","stage":"factor"}],"honest_boundary":"The positivity location is exact (identities) — but it is a location result, not a mechanism for new zero information; noting the signs are an expansion artifact does not by itself push zeros anywhere.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D2","rule":"−ζ′/ζ(s)=ΣΛ(n)n^{−s}, Λ≥0; log ζ(s)=Σ_{p,k}1/(kp^{ks})>0 (real s>1); δ(z)=∏_{p≤z}(1−1/p)>0 with −log δ(z)=ΣΣ1/(kp^k) a manifestly positive sum.","subtitle":"Positivity lives in the primitive (9a)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"−log δ(z) positive sum at z=10,30,100,1000","expected":"6 digits; δ(1000)=0.080965"},{"check":"δ(X)>0 monotone decreasing →0 vs A(X)=Σ_{d≤X}μ(d)/d oscillating","expected":"+0.0311, +0.0044, −0.0021, −0.0005 at X=10²…10⁵ — same limit 0; signs live only in the additive presentation"}]},{"checksum":"a2a373d2534c8fc8bb4e796cfa4f74a3934db8acaa40ad1175bfa091f937c89c","generates":[{"prescription":"Since 3+4cosθ+cos2θ=2(1+cosθ)²≥0 and −ζ′/ζ=ΣΛ(n)n^{−s} has positive coefficients, form the nonnegative 3-4-1 combination.","stage":"nonnegative combo"},{"prescription":"A zero on Re(s)=1 would cancel the 3/(σ−1) pole as σ→1⁺ — impossible inside a nonnegative sum.","stage":"contradiction"}],"honest_boundary":"Classical proof (cited, re-verified here) — 'positivity constrains zeros' is the classical 3-4-1 zero-free line, not a new result; the contribution is the miniature framing.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D3","rule":"3+4cosθ+cos2θ=2(1+cosθ)²≥0; 3(−ζ′/ζ)(σ)+4Re(−ζ′/ζ)(σ+it)+Re(−ζ′/ζ)(σ+2it)≥0 (σ>1).","subtitle":"3-4-1: positivity constrains zeros (Weil-shaped mechanism in miniature)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"Λ-sieve 3-4-1 sum on a t-grid","expected":"stays positive; grows 2.26→8.30→20.62 as σ→1⁺"}]},{"checksum":"711cfc420d6bdf5156c4a24bc123ee26c9941e2be3c461315853d562ba13dcb5","generates":[{"prescription":"Write −ζ′/ζ as a sum over the complex's vertex towers (prime powers): E₀(σ)=−ζ′/ζ(σ), E₁(σ,t)=−ζ′/ζ(σ+it), E₂(σ,t)=−ζ′/ζ(σ+2it).","stage":"towers"},{"prescription":"3+4cosθ+cos2θ=½|1+e^{iθ}|⁴ — the classical combination is a sum of manifestly nonnegative stratum energies e_{p,k}(σ,t)=½(log p)p^{−kσ}|1+p^{ikt}|⁴≥0.","stage":"fourth power"},{"prescription":"If ζ(1+it₀)=0 of order m≥1, then 4ReE₁(σ,t₀)~−4m/(σ−1)→−∞: negative infinite total energy built from nonnegative strata is impossible. (ReE₂ can only worsen it.)","stage":"restated proof"}],"honest_boundary":"Does NOT eliminate the analysis — the singularity structure (residue −m at a zero) is an analytic fact the complex houses but does not derive. Same traffic, new bridge, one genuinely new visible feature: no new theorem yet. 9c (stronger positivity → a new zero-free region) remains the real test.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"E(σ,t)=½Σ_pΣ_k(log p)p^{−kσ}|1+p^{ikt}|⁴=3E₀(σ)+4ReE₁(σ,t)+ReE₂(σ,t)≥0 termwise; E₀(σ)~1/(σ−1) is infinite total prime energy at σ=1.","subtitle":"The zero-free line in the energy language (9b — the bridge carries traffic)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"two forms agree on a (σ,t) grid (zero_free.py)","expected":"6 digits, everywhere"},{"check":"E₀ at σ=2→1.2","expected":"0.57→4.02; at t=14.1347 (first-zero height), σ=1.2: ReE₁=−1.06, ReE₂=+0.47 — bounded, no −m/(σ−1) divergence"}]},{"checksum":"0fefb64880c78b86373646b50ceed6bbb10297ac2f56d8eeb92a0f808f18522b","from":"D2","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"D1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"e44f5d2687ec71f686cf172c3c80114793124075cb714fe6d66255a1a3156ef2","from":"D4","id":"L2","rel":"implements","to":"D3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"38dcc7f828959f12c588d415bf3290cc7963987b15859bd96d6c7a1f054465df","from":"D4","id":"L3","rel":"supports","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"f6c133eed98e3d98faf44e81655ef8e4fa684b2e26d14cab58b2c5288b250f42","from":"C2","id":"L4","rel":"depends_on","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"4f21d4d101bca84cd6c37ea9714e435d50f8031600dce3bdc9026e31e2771e5d","consequence":"The complete classical argument — Dirichlet series, trig positivity, pole/zero singularity structure — is expressible in the sieve's language with the contradiction made visible (termwise nonnegativity versus a required negative divergence); 9c remains the real test.","id":"V1","note":"Honest verdict: same traffic, new bridge, one genuinely new visible feature — no new theorem yet. 9b was stepping stone #2: can the sieve's geometry carry the classical zero-free line — answered yes.","status":"exact","subject":"9b — the bridge carries traffic","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","V1":"V"},"wire_checksum":"30e41055deff3faa0335e5aabfcc73bd36fe8edc520d2182157b8a9a3228e9cf"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1